menu "V2X Base"

config MCUX_COMPONENT_component.v2x_base
    bool "v2x_base"
    select MCUX_COMPONENT_driver.mu1
    help
      EdgeLock V2X base (debug) service driver. Ported from the Linux
      drivers/firmware/imx/v2x_base_msg.c, it implements the four V2X base
      operations (start_rng, pwr_state, get_fw_version, debug_dump) over the
      message unit (via the generic fsl_mu driver) using the same enclave message framing as ele_crypto
      and v2x_crypto, with the V2X debug command tag (0x17) and version (0x02).


config V2X_FW_IMG_DDR_ADDR
    hex "V2X firmware image DDR address"
    default 0x8b000000
    depends on MCUX_COMPONENT_component.v2x_base
    help
      No prefix in generated macro
      Physical DDR address of the V2X firmware image that the EdgeLock
      enclave (ELE) authenticates and releases during V2X bring-up
      (ELE_BaseAPI_V2xFwAuthenticate). The image must have been loaded to
      this address before the V2X debug / FCE message units will answer
      (default 0x8b000000 on the i.MX943 EVK).

endmenu
